705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (This part of our project manages the automatic refilling and draining of the water tank. When the water level is low, the system activates the inlet valve to refill the tank; if the tank is at risk of overflowing, the outlet valve is triggered to release excess water. The decision-making process is based on the readings from nine water level sensors, which provide real-time input to determine whether to add or reduce water.)
/E (This part of our project manages the automatic refilling and draining of the water tank. When the water level is low, the system activates the inlet valve to refill the tank; if the tank is at risk of overflowing, the outlet valve is triggered to release excess water. The decision-making process is based on the readings from nine water level sensors, which provide real-time input to determine whether to add or reduce water.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
